# Cycle 1 Batch C hygiene (Item 5): ad-hoc analyzer dumps, Node/pptx sidecar
# files, and the OpenCode installer script are local-only and must stay
# untracked. Signing keystores must live outside the repo (see android
# release-signing docs); the *.jks / key.properties rules above already cover
# nested paths, and the entries below guard the repo root explicitly.
/analysis.txt
/analyze_out.txt
/analyze_output.txt
/tutorial/frames_concat.txt
/package.json
/package-lock.json
/install.sh
/upload-keystore.jks
/key.properties

# Cycle 5 F3c/F5/F7 hygiene: tutorial generated outputs + media are
# local-only and must stay untracked. Source scripts (tutorial/*.py and
# tutorial docs) stay tracked. History is not rewritten; this only guards
# the worktree going forward.
# Cycle 6 P1 hygiene: agent working files (.opencode/plans, tasks, debug,
# loop-criteria, agents, skills, opencode.json, orchestrator-subagents) are
# local-only and must stay untracked. History is not rewritten.
.opencode/
.opencode/acm-options-debug.json
